_np = [['Trace the flow of money in a simple diagram from lender to platform to borrower and back, and mark where the platform earns a fee and where each risk sits.', 'Note that unlike a savings account, the money lent may not be protected, so lenders can lose some or all of it if borrowers fail to repay.'], ['Practise with a sample loan of 1,000 currency units over 12 months at 8 percent, calculate the monthly payment and total interest, and compare the result with a 6-month term.', 'Always compare loans using the total amount repaid and the yearly rate on the same basis, rather than the headline monthly figure alone.'], ['Build a simple scorecard using income stability, existing debts and repayment history, give each a score from 1 to 5, and set a clear cut-off for acceptance.', 'Spread lending across many small loans rather than a few large ones, because one default then affects only a small share of the total.'], ['Build a spreadsheet that applies an assumed default rate, such as 4 percent, and a fee to expected interest, then compare net return under three different default rates.', 'Test a bad case where defaults double, and check whether lenders would still be treated fairly and the platform could cover its running costs.'], ['Explain the loan terms to borrowers in plain language, including the total repaid, the late fees and what happens if a payment is missed.', 'Avoid pressuring anyone to borrow more than they can afford, and set a limit such as repayments no higher than a stated share of income.'], ['Show lenders the risks in clear words before they commit, including a statement that returns are not guaranteed, and keep a record that they have read it.', 'Check which local rules apply to platforms that arrange loans, and treat this course as learning material rather than advice on how to operate lawfully.'], ['Set up daily checks that payments received match payments due, and keep a log of exceptions with a note on who resolved each one and when.', 'Define a clear process for late payments: reminder at day 3, a call at day 10, and a written plan offered before any further action.'], ['Present your platform concept in five slides covering problem, how it works, risks, numbers and fairness, with one worked example of a single loan.', 'Ask a reviewer to look for weak points in your assumptions, and revise the model after each round of questions.']]
