C['intro_add'] = ['You will draw the flow of money between lender, platform and borrower and mark each fee and risk, so you can explain how the model works to a newcomer.', 'You will calculate monthly payment, total interest and total repaid for a sample loan, which lets you compare costs on the same basis instead of headline rates.', 'You will build a simple scorecard and explain why spreading small loans limits the damage of any single default, so credit risk becomes something you can reason about.', 'You will model net lender return under three default rates and a bad case, showing why optimistic returns can disappear when borrowers fail to repay.', 'You will explain loan terms in plain words and set repayment limits relative to income, helping a platform treat borrowers fairly and avoid pushing them into unaffordable debt.', 'You will write clear lender risk statements and note where local rules may apply, so the concept presents honest information and avoids implying guaranteed returns.', 'You will design daily payment checks, an exceptions log and a staged late-payment process, giving the platform a repeatable way to catch problems early.', 'You will present a five-slide concept with one worked loan example and respond to reviewer challenges, which shows whether your assumptions can survive scrutiny.']
